Article 9
Neglect as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (2) letter d is caused by:
a. acts that result in the failure to fulfill the needs of children properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or look after children as appropriate, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
c. acts of neglecting a person within the household sphere, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to an agreement or contract they are obliged to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to that person; and/or
d. acts that result in economic dependence by means of restricting and/or prohibiting decent work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.

Article 15
(1) The organizational structure of PPT as referred to in Article 14 consists of:
a. Chairperson;
b. Vice Chairperson;
c. Secretary; and
d. Members.
(2) The fields within the organizational structure of PPT at minimum include:
a. complaint service field;
b. health service field;
c. legal aid and law enforcement service field; d. social rehabilitation service field; and
e. repatriation and social reintegration field.

